From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer patch: use a locked fence for DMB ISH on AMD

Unity's render thread runs DMB ISH in its work-stealing queue. AMD's MFENCE
orders memory and serializes instruction execution. A locked RMW on a private
host word supplies the full load and store ordering required by DMB ISH. Use
LOCK NOTL to avoid changing registers or flags in either translation tier.
Keep MFENCE for other full barrier scopes, DSB, STLR, and non-AMD hosts.
Module libberberis_arm64.

diff --git a/cpu_emulation/assembler/instructions/insn_def_x86.json b/cpu_emulation/assembler/instructions/insn_def_x86.json
index b16e69976febb16bef264d11f15d66462058b214..25c7035d465df05db55671aa2d7d692daa4552df 100644
--- a/cpu_emulation/assembler/instructions/insn_def_x86.json
+++ b/cpu_emulation/assembler/instructions/insn_def_x86.json
@@ -1784,6 +1784,14 @@
         { "class": "FLAGS", "usage": "def" }
       ]
     },
+    {
+      "encodings": {
+        "Lock Notl": { "opcodes": [ "F0", "F7", "2" ] }
+      },
+      "args": [
+        { "class": "Mem32", "usage": "use_def" }
+      ]
+    },
     {
       "encodings": {
         "Lock Xaddb": { "opcodes": [ "F0", "0F", "C0" ], "type": "reg_to_rm" },
